      { t: "Step 1 \u2014 The name", d: "Baihui means \'Hundred Meetings\' \u2014 the texts say a hundred channels converge at the crown (Traditional). Whether or not you buy the number, the image is precise: this is the summit of the body\'s energy map, the point where everything rising arrives. The crown is the body\'s skylight \u2014 Baihui is the latch." },
      { t: "Step 2 \u2014 Finding it on your body", d: "Place a fingertip on the very top of your head. The classical landmark: draw a line from the top of one ear over the crown to the other ear \u2014 Baihui sits on the midline where that line crosses. You\'ll feel a slight soft spot or dip. If your head were a globe, this is the north pole." },
      { t: "Step 3 \u2014 How to work it", d: "Two methods. TAPPING: tap lightly with all fingertips for 30 seconds \u2014 like rain on the crown. This wakes it up. PRESSING: press firmly with one fingertip or the heel of the palm for 1 minute \u2014 this settles and regulates. Tapping lifts, pressing grounds-through-the-top. Choose by feel: foggy and heavy → tap; buzzy and overstimulated → press." },
      { t: "Step 4 \u2014 What it does", d: "Traditional claims: lifts depressive, heavy energy; clears brain fog; regulates the rising and falling of energy in the head; connects the crown flow (Traditional). Practitioners report a distinct \'clearing\' sensation \u2014 like a window opening at the top of the skull. The teaching\'s frame: when energy pools stagnant in the head (brain fog, heaviness, gloom), the crown is the drain and the chimney at once." },
      { t: "Step 5 \u2014 The theory behind it", d: "Baihui is GV20 \u2014 point 20 on the Governing Vessel, the midline channel that runs up the spine and over the crown (Traditional). The Governing Vessel is the sea of all yang channels: warming, lifting, activating. Working Baihui is working the master switch of the body\'s upward current. That\'s why it pairs with everything below it \u2014 it\'s the top of the circuit." },
      { t: "Step 6 \u2014 When to use it in your practice", d: "(1) BRAIN FOG: tap for 30 seconds before study, work, or any practice needing clarity. (2) HEAVY/DEPRESSIVE states: press firmly for a minute \u2014 the tradition says it lifts what sinks (Traditional). (3) AFTER deep meditation: a few taps \'closes\' the session and brings you back to the room. (4) WITH Yintang: the full vertical axis \u2014 brow then crown, bottom to top." },
      { t: "Step 7 \u2014 Pairings", d: "Baihui + Yongquan (sole of foot): the longest circuit in the body \u2014 crown to sole, heaven to earth. Work both and feel the whole column. Baihui + Yintang: the head axis for mental clarity. Baihui + Zusanli (below knee): lift the crown while building the legs\' stamina \u2014 clarity with staying power." },
      { t: "Step 8 \u2014 Safety", d: "Gentle point, no major contraindications. One caution from the tradition: if you already feel buzzy, overstimulated, or \'too high\' after energy work, prefer PRESSING over tapping \u2014 tapping adds lift to a system that needs settling (Traditional). And never hammer it: the crown responds to invitation, not assault." }
