      { t: "Step 6 \u2014 When to use it in your practice", d: "(1) HEADACHES: the first resort \u2014 1 minute each hand, and reassess. (2) STRESS: squeeze it during tense moments; the strong sensation gives the mind something to anchor on besides the worry. (3) BEFORE energy work: clears the head\'s static so the session starts clean. (4) JAW/FACE tension: the command point of the face \u2014 clenchers, grinders, scowlers, this is yours." },
      { t: "Step 7 \u2014 Pairings", d: "Hegu + Taichong (foot): the \'Four Gates\' \u2014 the most famous point combination in the tradition, opening the body\'s energy flow top and bottom (Traditional). Hegu + Yintang: headache protocol \u2014 hand point plus brow point. Hegu + Fengchi (base of skull): the full head-and-neck release for tension headaches." },
      { t: "Step 8 \u2014 Safety: the one rule", d: "AVOID IN PREGNANCY. The tradition holds that strong stimulation of LI4 can encourage uterine contraction (Traditional caution) \u2014 this is the most repeated safety rule in acupressure, and the app repeats it plainly: if you are or might be pregnant, skip this point. Everyone else: the only risk is pressing a nerve \u2014 sharp or electric means reposition." }
